    "Question #: 4": {
      "Title": "Exam 70-466 topic 1 question 89 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "DRAG DROP -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You are using Multidimensional Expressions (MDX) to query a SQL Server Analysis Services (SSAS) cube."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You need to compute the aggregate value of the 10 most-ordered produces in the Product Categories hierarchy. The Product level is the lowest in the hierarchy."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which functions should you use to complete the MDX query? (To answer, drag the appropriate functions from the list of functions to the correct locations in the answer area.)"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Select and Place:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/02155/0013100001.jpg"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {},
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer:"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/02155/0013200001.jpg"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Note:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "* Example (order of TopCount and Aggregate):"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "WITH -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "SET -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "[Top25Customers] as"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "TopCount([Customers].[All Customers].Children, 25.0, [Measures].[Sales])"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "MEMBER [Customers].[All Customers].[Rest of Customers] as"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Aggregate(Except([Customers].[All Customers].Children,[Top25Customers]))"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "SELECT -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "NON EMPTY {CROSSJOIN([Markets].[All Markets].Children,{[Measures].Sales})}"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "ON COLUMNS,"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Union([Top25Customers],{[Customers].[All Customers].[Rest of Customers]}) ON ROWS from [SteelWheelsSales]"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "* TopCount: Sorts a set in descending order and returns the specified number of elements with the highest values."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "*Aggregate:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Returns a number that is calculated by aggregating over the cells returned by the set expression. If a numeric expression is not provided, this function aggregates each measure within the current query context by using the default aggregation operator that is specified for each measure. If a numeric expression is provided, this function first evaluates, and then sums, the numeric expression for each cell in the specified set."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "* Example:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "One can extract the leaf members of a parent child hierarchy by asking the descendants of the root member with the following expression:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Descendants([Organization].[Organizations].&[1], , LEAVES)"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "* Incorrect:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "/ Not TopSUM: Returns, in order of decreasing rank, the top-most rows of a table whose cumulative total is at least a specified value."
          }
        ]
      },
